{
    "background_story": "Boden was a rugged outdoorsman with a penchant for storytelling. Growing up in the Appalachian Mountains, he learned the art of spinning yarns from his grandfather, a masterful tale-spinner. Boden's stories often began with the phrase 'I knew a fella...' and would weave a spell of adventure and danger around his listeners. One of his most famous tales was about a mysterious figure known only as 'Shirttail Bill,' a ghostly outlaw who roamed the woods, always staying one step ahead of the law. Boden's tales of Shirttail Bill's exploits became legendary in the region, with some claiming to have seen the ghostly figure themselves. Boden's stories kept the spirit of Shirttail Bill alive, and his own reputation as a master storyteller was cemented.",
